&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Join our Movement and Champion Restaurant Culture! 💚&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At TheFork we believe that the best things in life happen around the table. &lt;br&gt;As the leading restaurant booking platform in Europe, we connect the broadest community of loyal diners with the world’s favorite restaurants. Powered by innovation and a deep passion for the restaurant industry, we create unique dining experiences across 11 countries.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re part of the Tripadvisor Group and proud to be building a diverse, people-first culture where “respect”, “ownership”, “growth” and “better together” values thrive. &lt;br&gt;If you’re passionate about food, technology, and making a real impact, your seat at the table is ready.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;👉&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.careers.thefork.com&quot;&gt; Discover life at TheFork&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;This position offers a gross TTC annual salary range between 67.000€ and 73.000€, in line with the collective bargaining agreement and the company compensation philosophy. The final offer will reflect the candidate’s experience, qualifications, and the specific responsibilities of the role.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will do:&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead and develop the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, coach and motivate the CPS Trainers and Team Leaders, creating a high-performing and engaged team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set clear objectives and monitor performance through regular team meetings, individual follow-ups and coaching.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop the team’s skills through continuous feedback, coaching and structured development plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead a cultural shift within the CPS team, embedding a few simple, high-impact daily habits that improve restaurant partners’ adoption and perception of TheFork Manager.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay close to the field by regularly joining or delivering restaurant trainings, keeping a direct understanding of partner needs and team challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support key people processes including recruitment, onboarding, performance reviews and talent development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster a culture of ownership, collaboration, continuous improvement and customer obsession.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive training strategy and operational excellence&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and continuously evolve the training strategy for restaurant partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Influence the definition of clear objectives, priorities and success metrics for the training activity, in partnership with SalesOps team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and implement a continuous training framework, defining content, formats, tools and cadence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure consistent training standards and methodologies across the team and markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to simplify processes and improve the efficiency and impact of the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn data, partner feedback and field observations into concrete actions to improve adoption and engagement with TheFork Manager.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor key performance indicators and use them to prioritize initiatives and drive continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborate across TheFork&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with local and Central teams including Sales, Account Management, Sales Operations, Product, Operations and Marketing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build strong alignment between CPS and other restaurant-facing teams to ensure a consistent partner experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gather structured feedback from restaurant partners and the CPS team and translate it into actionable insights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a strong voice of the restaurant partner towards Product and Central teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner regularly with Product teams to share insights, identify friction points and contribute to the continuous improvement of TheFork Manager.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Share best practices across markets and contribute to cross-country initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You Must Meet These Critical Qualifications &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have minimum 3-4 years of previous experience in driving customer adoption/usage of a SaaS solution, preferably in restaurants/hospitality sector.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are proficient with Salesforce and/or other CRM tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have solid people management experience and a proven ability to coach, develop and engage teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a strong customer mindset and are passionate about creating an outstanding experience for restaurant partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are results-oriented and comfortable working with KPIs, targets and performance management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You combine strong analytical skills with a pragmatic, hands-on approach.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are comfortable leading change and translating a strategic vision into simple, repeatable actions for your team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are proactive, autonomous and comfortable making decisions in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have excellent communication and influencing skills and can work effectively with multiple stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are fluent in English and comfortable working in an international and multicultural environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are interested in technology, digital products and the restaurant industry.&lt;/li&gt;
