&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Senior Marketing Manager, Loyalty to grow and strengthen our rewards programs across Tripadvisor and Viator — someone who can set strategic direction and execute against it. This role is 100% dedicated to Loyalty and works closely with product, engineering, analytics, and CRM. You&#39;ll move between strategy, campaign execution, and analysis depending on what the work needs day to day.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location: East Coast- United States&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the loyalty marketing strategy. Define and evolve the Tripadvisor Rewards value proposition and tiering strategy, and shape how the program shows up to members.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run the campaign engine. Plan and execute always-on and calendared campaigns — Welcome Offer optimization, sales events (e.g., Travel Deal Tuesday), sweepstakes, challenges, and partner-funded promotions — across paid and owned channels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead cross-functionally. Drive alignment with product, engineering, design, and analytics to test and launch new program mechanics, from offer targeting to member perks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the business case with data. Use booking and program data — member behavior, redemption, tier progression, holdout/incrementality results — to prioritize what to build next and prove out ROI to leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Measure what matters. Work with analytics to run and interpret holdout/control tests, and translate results into clear go/no-go calls and next steps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Benchmark the competition. Track best-in-class loyalty programs (e.g., Starbucks, Nike, Sephora) to inform our approach to tiering, gamification, and member value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Do the work at every level. Set strategy one day, brief creative or QA an offer the next.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
