&lt;li&gt;5+ years of hands-on marketing experience working across the full spectrum from strategy to execution — in travel, e-commerce, subscription, or retail. You are equally able to build a program vision and ship a campaign.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of product marketing work — translating product capabilities into clear member-facing value propositions and go-to-market plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills — comfortable working with data - either in partnership with analytics and data science teams or working independently - to define metrics and interpret test results. You should be able to pull your own data using AI tools and dashboards.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to use AI tools to improve efficiency, quality, and decision-making in day-to-day work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to operate effectively with a global-first mindset&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven track record of cross-functional leadership — driving alignment and momentum across product, engineering, design, analytics, and CRM in a fast-paced, iterative environment; comfort operating with ambiguity and evolving scope.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A bias for action and comfort working with limited resources.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills; able to flex between an executive-level strategy narrative and a detailed campaign brief.&lt;/li&gt;
